  "interpretation": [
    "Production HTTP tests hold the provider response until POST returns a durable job ID. They prove measured charges, missing-usage capacity retention, measured provider failures, and insufficient-budget refusal before dispatch.",
    "A provider estimate of USD 0.99 cannot replace the pinned USD 0.375 charge for five measured output seconds.",
    "Receipt recovery tests use memory, real synchronous Badger, real Valkey, and filesystem blobs. They recreate service objects after failed writes or lost acknowledgements. They do not kill operating-system processes.",
    "Receipt corruption tests refuse changed account identity, measurement identity, invalid length, and altered asset bytes before job completion.",
    "Background tests cover caller disconnect, worker saturation, shutdown, execution expiry, and valuation copy isolation. Expiry leaves unknown provider work unresolved.",
    "Native operation deadlines preserve the ordinary executor deadline and its other policies.",
    "Current code uses job schema 4. Batch schema 2, attempt payload 2, claim payload 3, and window/history payload 1 remain unchanged."
  ],
  "earlier_failures": [
    "The first reporting check failed compilation because Cost requires usage.Cost rather than float64. The repair preserves integer nano-USD.",
    "The first production run returned a job ID but sent zero provider calls. Credential destination compilation omitted exact-model overrides.",
    "The first destination test selected an acquisition-only credential profile. This fixture failure does not prove the production defect. destination-before-valid.jsonl reproduces the endpoint refusal with the correct inference profile.",
    "Architecture tests required registration of the ninth protocol and rejected connector-owned deadlines. The connector now requires the execution deadline. No deadline guard was weakened."
  ],
  "verification_limits": [
    "The broad race run predates the final corruption and executor timing tests. Separate focused race and pure-Go runs cover those additions.",
    "TestContainerRecipePersistence skipped because its opt-in condition was absent. This result does not qualify the replicated container recipe.",
    "Full OPERATOR-GUIDE lint reports pre-existing findings. The changed prose and four new production source files pass their separate prose checks.",
    "External video asset URLs remain references only. Separate destination approval and bounded recovery downloads remain required.",
    "No further paid inference ran. The provider test uses local HTTP fixtures.",
    "PostgreSQL, multiple-process loss, failover, capacity, A47, full paid-operation matrix, native CI, pre-PR review, exact published dependency pin, and paired merges remain unqualified.",
